Replay identity and capture
---------------------------
Both replays loaded Linux, reached `retired=2,999,999,998`, and stopped with
`exit_kind=budget_exhausted`. For each nonce, the full stop object, UART bytes,
all entry samples and all retained source stride-512 poll samples match the
corresponding automatic source run exactly. UART length is 23,356 bytes in
both runs. Direct replay remains diagnostic; the automatic source comparison
still has `matches=false` for machine observations and ordered UART.

Schema v10 captured exactly two clock records at the selected entry RIP per
run; `clock_trace_missing=0`, entry omissions and poll sample omissions are
zero. Run 0001 has 43,871 entry hits and 66,395 stride samples; run 0002 has
43,868 entry hits and 66,389 stride samples. Neither trace changed execution
semantics or comparator rules.

Pre-charge callback ledger
--------------------------
`tsc_hz=1,000,000,000`; all snapshots have `initial_now_ns=0`.
`retired_ns_charged` is the retired-instruction time already committed by
completed quanta. It deliberately excludes the current quantum, which is
charged only after the CPU run returns. Therefore its difference is **not** a
claim that the guest executed exactly that many more instructions by the
callback.

| Run | Entry hit | Callback TSC | `now_ns` | Retired ns charged | PM ns | PIT ns | RDTSC ns charged | Idle ns | Quantum | IRQs |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 0001 | 1 | `0x6181dbee` | 1,635,900,398 | 1,524,205,398 | 0 | 16,673,000 | 95,022,000 | 0 | 136,012 | 0 |
| 0002 | 1 | `0x6182ac5c` | 1,635,953,756 | 1,524,256,756 | 0 | 16,673,000 | 95,024,000 | 0 | 136,014 | 0 |
| 0001 | 2 | `0x61822f6c` | 1,635,921,772 | 1,524,224,772 | 0 | 16,673,000 | 95,024,000 | 0 | 136,014 | 0 |
| 0002 | 2 | `0x6182ffa4` | 1,635,975,076 | 1,524,276,076 | 0 | 16,673,000 | 95,026,000 | 0 | 136,016 | 0 |

For entry hit 1 the callback-TSC gap is 53,358 cycles. The ledger explains
that clock gap arithmetically as +51,358 already-charged retired ns and
+2,000 already-charged RDTSC ns; initial, PM, PIT, idle and delivered-IRQ
values are equal. Both component sums exactly equal their `now_ns`, with
`unaccounted_elapsed_ns=0`. This localizes the observed early clock offset to
charged-time components, but not why the retired path or earlier RDTSC count
differs. It does not establish nonce causality or benignity.

Between entry hits 1 and 2, run 0001 advances 21,374 ns and run 0002 advances
21,320 ns. Each ledger advances 2,000 ns in already-charged RDTSC ticks; the
remaining advances are 19,374 and 19,320 ns of already-charged retired time.
This agrees with the observed entry-to-entry TSC intervals, while preserving
the same pre-charge caveat.

The final `virtual_ns` values still diverge (37,404,144,074 versus
37,401,694,078), so the first-entry ledger does not explain later execution,
UART ordering, or the strict comparator failure.

